From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: insert PMKR1Name into the per-link RSNEs for the FT Reassociation Response MIC

The FTE MIC of the Reassociation Response frame sent to a non-AP MLD is
calculated over the RSNE of each affiliated AP for the requested links.
Those RSNEs are the ones the non-AP MLD sees in the frame, i.e., with
PMKID = PMKR1Name, and not the RSNEs as advertised in the Beacon frames
(this is also what wlantest does when it verifies the MIC). The AP MLD
side used the Beacon frame RSNEs, so the MIC never matched: a non-AP MLD
completed the FT protocol, then immediately sent an unprotected
Deauthentication frame and fell back to a full SAE authentication.

Insert PMKR1Name into each affiliated AP's RSNE before including it in
the MIC calculation.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
@@ -2247,6 +2247,11 @@
  * RSNEs (or RSNXEs, if rsnxe) of the affiliated APs of the AP MLD for the
  * links negotiated by the STA, concatenated in increasing link ID order. The
  * number of elements included is returned in *count.
+ *
+ * The RSNE of each affiliated AP is included with PMKID = PMKR1Name inserted,
+ * i.e., in the form in which the non-AP MLD sees it in the Reassociation
+ * Response frame (IEEE Std 802.11be, 13.8.5), not as advertised in the Beacon
+ * frame.
  */
 static struct wpabuf * wpa_ft_mlo_link_rsn_ies(struct wpa_state_machine *sm,
 					       bool rsnxe, unsigned int *count)
@@ -2255,7 +2260,7 @@
 	unsigned int link_id;
 
 	*count = 0;
-	buf = wpabuf_alloc(MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS * 257);
+	buf = wpabuf_alloc(MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS * (257 + 2 + PMKID_LEN));
 	if (!buf)
 		return NULL;
 
@@ -2263,6 +2268,8 @@
 		const struct mld_link *link = &sm->mld_links[link_id];
 		const struct wpa_authenticator *la = link->wpa_auth;
 		const u8 *ie;
+		u8 rsne_buf[257 + 2 + PMKID_LEN];
+		size_t rsne_len;
 
 		if (!link->valid || !la)
 			continue;
@@ -2270,7 +2277,23 @@
 			    rsnxe ? WLAN_EID_RSNX : WLAN_EID_RSN);
 		if (!ie)
 			continue;
-		wpabuf_put_data(buf, ie, 2 + ie[1]);
+		if (rsnxe) {
+			wpabuf_put_data(buf, ie, 2 + ie[1]);
+			(*count)++;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		rsne_len = 2 + ie[1];
+		os_memcpy(rsne_buf, ie, rsne_len);
+		if (wpa_insert_pmkid(rsne_buf, &rsne_len, sm->pmk_r1_name,
+				     true) < 0) {
+			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+				   "FT: Failed to insert PMKR1Name into the RSNE of link %u",
+				   link_id);
+			wpabuf_free(buf);
+			return NULL;
+		}
+		wpabuf_put_data(buf, rsne_buf, rsne_len);
 		(*count)++;
 	}
 
